  "body": "## What happens\n\n`onOpen` of the Fanuc lathe post writes `G21 G18 G40 G80 G99` (or `G20 ...`) on one block. The Fanuc operator's manual says to specify G20/G21 alone in a block at the start of the program. The Fanuc mill posts already write the unit word on its own block (#901).\n\n## Expected\n\n`G20` or `G21` is on its own block. The other modal words follow on the next block.\n\n## Evidence (upstream main `eafe6aec6`)\n\n- `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps:457`: `block([inch ? \"G20\" : \"G21\", \"G18\", \"G40\", \"G80\", \"G99\"])`.\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps:596-598`: `unitBlock()` writes the unit alone.\n- FANUC Series 0i-F operator's manual B-64604EN-1/01 (inch/metric conversion).\n\nFound by the post audit against the Fanuc manuals (#4130).\n\n## Done means\n\nThe fanuc-lathe goldens show `G21` (or `G20`) alone on its block, followed by `G18 G40 G80 G99`.\n",
